<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Red River Expedition (1870)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1870">1870</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Wolseley Expedition</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Red River Expedition of 1870 was a military force of British regulars and Canadian militia led by Colonel <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garnet-wolseley">Garnet Wolseley</a> to assert Canadian authority at Red River, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manitoba">Manitoba</a>, after the resistance led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-riel">Louis Riel</a>. The troops travelled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ontario">Ontario</a> by lake, river and portage and reached Fort Garry in August 1870, finding that Riel had fled.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/red-river-expedition-1870.jpg" alt="Red River Expedition (1870)" width="320" height="197" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Frances Anne Hopkins · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FAH_Red_River_Expedition.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
